<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amyntas III of Macedon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 370 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amyntas III was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> from about 393 to 370 BCE and father of Philip II. His reign was beset by Illyrian invasions and rival claimants, and the Chalcidian League led by Olynthus seized much of his kingdom, including Pella, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> intervened and broke the league in 379 BCE. He held his kingdom together through alliances with Sparta and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amyntas-iii-of-macedon.jpg" alt="Amyntas III of Macedon" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matia.gr · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Amyntas_III-161113.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
